          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: At 3:00 AM on June 16, 1982, witnesses observed in the sky a spherical object with a halo, followed by a cluster of smaller points of yellow-orange color forming a glowing trail. This ensemble moved slowly in a straight line from northeast to southeast. The observation lasted less than a minute, and no noise associated with the phenomenon was heard. Based on descriptions of the phenomenon, these individuals likely witnessed an atmospheric reentry.",
